''               LEFT's. The where token gains NOMOTION. No existing record changes shape
''               25 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=45, FMT 29: task 3621 (R20.1 part 3, DOCs/plans/DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md SS6). The
''               driver now reports why a drive ended (getStopReason()) and what it handled on its own (getEvent()), and
''               start() refuses a start check that still fails after its retries. Cog 0 reads the event log by DRAINING
''               it (evDrain()): every event is printed as the new BM-EV and folded into the cell that judges it. New
''               cells: FAULTRESP -- R20-DUAL-SR-FAULT, R20-DUAL-SR-FLOST, R20-DUAL-SR-PARTNER, R20-DUAL-FRONTST-EV and
''               R20-T0-EV-LATE (new records BM-SR, BM-FRONTST after each FLTPLAT trial); part D -- R20-DUAL-EV-FOLDBACK,
''               R20-DUAL-EV-CLIMIT, R20-DUAL-EV-PATH and R20-T0-EV-LATE (new BM-EVTOT); START -- R20-DUAL-REFUSE, -OPTOUT,
''               -RETRY, -NOREFUSE, -EV-WALKGUARD, -EV-HALLMISSED, -EV-HALLILL and R20-PACK-EV, each in its own build.
''               START_NEG_PHASE's lifetimes (now 12) rotate three ways: opt-out (setStartChecks(FALSE), where PHNEG-X and
''               WINDNEG-X are judged exactly as before), refusal, and withhold-first. dual-start-nowalk opts out. A start
''               that returns -1 prints BM-SREFUSE (steering) or BM-REFUSE (a wheel): the cause from getError() and every
''               getHealth() mask. The stall watchdog allows a start its derived worst case, WD_START_GRACE_MS, on top of
''               WD_STALL_MS (BM-BUILD appends wd_start_ms). BM-SKHEALTH gains refuse, l_rec, r_rec and BM-SKNEG mode, each
''               just before why, which stays last.
''               The ABI dump names the 21-long status run (foldback_frames) and fault (BM-ABIS3 gains foldback_frames).
''               TOKMAX_CELL goes to 22 for the two longest R20 ids
''               25 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=46, FMT 30: PL-136 (task 3613, Visit 10 pass 4 sec 4a). PL-120's diagnostics now key
''               on a commanded wheel that does not move, in PREFLT too. In EVERY part, a PREFLT nudge with no hall tick
''               by FR_NOMOTION_MS dumps that driver's runs mid-nudge (BM-ABI* where,NOMOTION), and a nudge that does not
''               move emits its ring as a trace (BM-TRACE seg,PREFLT cause,START; in FAULTRESP every nudge is traced, the
''               moving ones as the in-run control). In part FAULTRESP only, a wheel whose nudge did not move is retried AT
''               ONCE in up to PF_RETRY_TRIES fresh lifetimes PF_RETRY_GAP_MS apart, each nudged, dumped and traced as the
''               first (new BM-PFRETRY per retry); when every retry fails and it is the only such wheel, the recovery probe
''               runs on it before FLTRESP (BM-FRRECOV seg,PREFLT). A wheel either stage moves is un-retired and runs its
''               trials. BM-TS gains u, v and w, the three phases the ring always carried apart (only their sum ph was
''               printed); BM-FRRECOV gains seg; BM-FRDIAG gains pf_tries and pf_gap_ms; BM-FRRECSUM gains l_pf, l_pf_rec,
''               l_pf_n, l_pf_try and the same for r_, and its recovered and tries print NA when the FLTRESP probe did not
