''               dual-start-swapneg keeps its last 3, SK_WALKS_SWAP), and after each walk prints a new BM-SKWLEG per wheel per
''               leg -- four a walk -- beside the ring-rebuilt BM-SKWALK, from the steering object's new testLeftGetWalkLeg() /
''               testRightGetWalkLeg(), read after the walk's rest confirm. It is a diagnostic: no cell judges it, and no
''               cell's criterion changes (R19-DUAL-WALK-X is now over 10 walks). The stall watchdog allows checkWiring() its
''               derived worst case, WD_WALK_GRACE_MS, as it allows a start its own: the steering walk runs its second leg
''               after a timed-out first, so two timed-out legs block cog 0 about 4.1 s, past WD_STALL_MS. BM-SKBUILD
''               appends wd_walk_ms
''               25 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=48, FMT 32: task 3611 (R20.4, DRIVER_REV 25). New part PACK (-D DUAL_PART_PACK,
''               tier dual-pack): the pack voltage sensor on Stephen's fitted unit, attended, nothing moves. One steering
''               lifetime: step 1 reads the pack steady for 60 s (BM-PKREAD, BM-PKSTEADY), steps 2-5 unplug and replug the
''               sensor at the pack twice, each ended by the sensor seeing it (BM-PKCYCLE), the first unplug marking the
