''               step RESTCOAST, after COOPSHUT, on two lifetimes of its own: both wheels at power D_RC_POWER (about
''               80 x 10^6), then steering.stop() alone -- the reference, a free coast -- and, in the second, stop() and
''               start() back to back. The instrument counts each wheel's hall ticks straight from the pins (source
''               INST_SRC_NONE, so it reads no library object across the stop and start) over RC_WINDOW_MS from the
''               stop. New cell R20-DUAL-RESTCOAST per wheel: FAIL when the restarted wheel keeps under RC_KEEP_PCT of
''               the reference's rate, which the pre-DRIVER_REV 27 low-side short through the ATN park would cause
